-0x0000e0f4,cm848_calculateAlphaAltitudeDerateLatch,Alpha altitude derate latch: returns 1 while alpha must follow altitude_derate_alpha (e2m 104B +8 Altitude_Derate_Alpha), else 0. With bit 0x20 of feature_enable_flags_cal clear it clears alpha_altitude_derate_timer (e2m 104A +1A Alpha_Altitude_Derate_Timer) and returns 0. Otherwise, in every pass final_fueling_state is FUELING_STATE_ALTITUDE_DERATE it reloads the timer with altitude_derate_alpha_timeout (e2m 104B +A Altitude_Derate_Alpha_Timeout, 'time alpha is latched to ADALF after Altitude Derate stops fuel limiting') and returns 1; after the derate stops it counts the timer down by 1 per pass and keeps returning 1 until the timer is 0. Only caller hpcr_calculateFuelTrimOutput: a nonzero result selects alpha source 2 (altitude). (was cm848_checkPressureFuelState)
-0x0000e164,cm848_calculateSensorEma
-0x0000e218,cm848_calculateAlphaOnGovernorResult,Alpha on governor result (e2m 104A +A Alpha_Governor, '[APGVAP] result of On Governor'): returns 1 while the engine is on a speed governor, that is final_fueling_state is FUELING_STATE_VEHICLE_SPEED_LIMIT or cruise_control_engaged_flag is 1, else 0. Called by timingProtectionFlagsOrchestrator when bit 0x2000 of governor_fault_status_flags (algorithm enable flags word 0) is set; the result is stored in fuel_rate_condition_status (0x40a172) and a 1 lets alpha_base ramp toward 1.0. (was cm848_checkFuelRateCondition)
-0x0000e248,cm848_calculateAlphaLowSpeedGovernorResult,Alpha low speed governor result (e2m 104A +C Alpha_LSG, '[APLSAP] result of LSG algorithm'): a timeout after the low speed governor last acted. While alpha_low_speed_governor_state_detected_flag is 1 it reloads alpha_low_speed_governor_timer (e2m 104A +16 Alpha_LSG_Timer) with low_speed_governor_alpha_timeout (e2m 104B +14 LSG_Alpha_Timeout, 'time that must expire without LSG commanding fuel before alpha is one'), sets alpha_low_speed_governor_timer_active_flag and returns 0; while the active flag is set and the timer is above 0 it counts it down by 1 per pass and returns 0; otherwise it clears the active flag and returns 1. Called by timingProtectionFlagsOrchestrator when bit 0x400 of governor_fault_status_flags (algorithm enable flags word 0) is set; the result is stored in pressure_fuel_delay_a_status (0x40a174) and a 1 lets alpha_base ramp toward 1.0. (was cm848_checkPressureFuelDelayA)
-0x0000e2cc,cm848_calculateAlphaAirFuelControlResult,Alpha air fuel control result (e2m 104A +6 Alpha_AFC, '[APAFSS] result of AFC algorithm'): a timeout after air fuel control (or the low speed governor) last limited the fuel. While alpha_air_fuel_control_state_detected_flag or alpha_low_speed_governor_state_detected_flag is 1 it reloads alpha_air_fuel_control_timer (e2m 104A +18 Alpha_AFC_Timer) with air_fuel_control_alpha_timeout (e2m 104B +6 AFC_Alpha_Timeout, 'time that must elapse without AFC limiting before ALPHA may be set to one'), sets alpha_air_fuel_control_timer_active_flag and returns 0; while the active flag is set and the timer is above 0 it counts it down by 1 per pass and returns 0; otherwise it clears the active flag and returns 1. Called by timingProtectionFlagsOrchestrator when bit 0x800 of governor_fault_status_flags (algorithm enable flags word 0) is set; the result is stored in pressure_fuel_delay_b_status (0x40a16e) and a 1 lets alpha_base ramp toward 1.0. (was cm848_checkPressureFuelDelayB)
-0x0000e360,cm848_calculateAlphaLowAmbientAirPressureResult,Alpha low ambient air pressure result (e2m 104A +12 Alpha_Low_Ambient_Air_Pressure, '[APAAPRSS] alpha based only on ambient air pressure logic'): a hysteresis on barometric_pressure_reference. Returns 1 (alpha may ramp to 1.0) while it is below alpha_lock_on_barometric_pressure (e2m 104B +10 Alpha_Lock_On_Air_Pressure, 'air pressure below which alpha is ramped to 1'), 0 once it is above alpha_lock_off_barometric_pressure (e2m 104B +E Alpha_Lock_Off_Air_Pressure, 'air pressure after hysteresis to unlock alpha'; ROM 1540 against 1507 for the lock on value), and the previous alpha_low_ambient_air_pressure_result in between. Called by timingProtectionFlagsOrchestrator when bit 0x8000 of governor_fault_status_flags (algorithm enable flags word 0) is set; the result is stored in alpha_low_ambient_air_pressure_result (0x40a17a). (was cm848_checkPressureHysteresis)
